WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.710
- The day today is an
ominous March 13th, 2020.

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:04.880
Why do I say ominous?

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:07.310
'Cause it is Friday the
13th, but not to worry.

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:11.110
In this video, we're gonna
remain alert, not anxious.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:11.943
I'm not gonna give you

00:00:11.943 --> 00:00:13.750
any number updates starting this video,

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:16.230
because I think the numbers
are horribly inaccurate,

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:19.010
especially here in the United
States for one main reason.

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:20.530
We don't have enough testing kits

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:23.180
to find out who actually has this virus.

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:24.720
But let's talk about it, you ready?

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.660
The WHO has officially
labeled this virus a pandemic.

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:30.640
Not really surprising, two videos ago,

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.150
we said that it was
technically a pandemic then,

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:34.570
now we have this label on it.

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:35.700
What does it mean for you?

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:37.780
Practically speaking, not much.

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:40.300
It means that this virus is
internationally spreading,

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.550
it can spread through
countries very easily,

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:43.990
there's more funding available,

00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:46.710
more communication happening
between health agencies.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:48.190
But on a day to day standpoint,

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:50.310
this pandemic label
shouldn't really affect you.

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:52.280
You may have noticed
there's closures happening,

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:54.790
cancellations happening
all across the board.

00:00:54.790 --> 00:00:58.070
In fact, I had five, six speaking
engagements get postponed.

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:01.650
Speaking at Johns Hopkins,
Yale, The College of New Jersey.

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:04.830
All of these have to take a
back seat for public safety.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:06.790
Now I know seeing all these cancellations

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:07.780
can get you worried,

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:09.550
but we're gonna stay alert not anxious.

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:11.800
Cancellations are a good thing.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:13.180
This is a public health measure

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:16.170
that actually shows solidarity
within our community.

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:17.690
Because when we shut down these events,

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:19.540
we limit how this virus spreads.

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:21.760
Why is it important to
limit this virus spread?

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:24.410
Because we have to offer
community protection

00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:26.070
to those who can't protect themselves.

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:27.350
This means the elderly,

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:29.600
those with serious medical
chronic conditions,

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:31.740
and those who are immunocompromised,

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:33.540
possibly because of a medical condition

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:35.180
or a medication they may be taking.

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:37.610
Traditionally we offer
this type of herd immunity,

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:39.920
or community protection through vaccines.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:42.750
Unfortunately we cannot
make a vaccine this quickly

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:46.250
and the WHO has stated the
earliest possible timeline

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:49.330
for this vaccine would happen mid 2021.

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:51.290
So we can't expect a vaccine soon,

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:53.460
but we are gonna be talking
about possible treatments

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:54.370
in the coming minutes.

00:01:54.370 --> 00:01:56.860
Another reason I've talked about on CNN

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:59.280
of why it's important to
limit community spread.

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:01.930
Because we do not want a run on hospitals.

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:04.920
In Italy they're experiencing
a tremendous need

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:06.640
for equipment, for doctors

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:08.690
because their hospitals
are getting overrun

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:12.200
with patients who need respiratory
support, who need fluids

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:13.720
and here in the United States,

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:16.460
we simply do not have enough ICU beds

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:19.040
if everyone is to get
this virus simultaneously.

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:22.540
So by slowing the rate at
which this virus infect others,

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:25.120
we're doing something
called flattening the curve.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:28.200
Traditionally when a population
of individuals gets sick,

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:29.870
there's a bell curve that happens.

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:32.570
What we like to do is flatten this curve.

00:02:32.570 --> 00:02:35.250
The way we do that is by
limiting crowded events.

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:37.440
Here in New York State,
we actually have a rule,

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:40.270
no events with greater
than 500 individuals.

00:02:40.270 --> 00:02:42.180
We're probably gonna see
that tighten even further

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:44.880
and I would not be surprised
to see schools shutdown.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:46.950
Because we want to flatten that curve,

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:48.510
we wanna decrease the spread,

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:50.010
so that our hospitals can manage

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:51.170
the individuals who are sick

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:53.590
and not run into a problem
like they have in Italy.

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:55.790
Many of my patients and
friends have been asking

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:57.860
about what they can do
to protect themselves

00:02:57.860 --> 00:02:59.210
from this novel coronavirus.

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:01.240
It's still personal responsibility.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:02.960
You have to not go out when you're sick,

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:05.190
you have to limit your
exposure to large crowds,

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:07.670
while you may have tickets
for a show you wanna see,

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:10.130
or maybe your sporting
event is still going on.

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:11.740
Try and limit that spread.

00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:14.930
The CDC put an urgent
warning out to those over 60,

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:16.960
I think that warning should
apply to more people.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.970
And again, it doesn't mean
we should be panicking.

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:21.600
This isn't a panicdemic,
this is a pandemic.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:23.970
What we should be doing is
staying alert, not anxious

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:26.780
and the way we do that is by
getting quality information

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:29.250
from sources like the WHO and CDC,

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:31.920
so that we can be best
informed to protect our health

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:33.310
and the health of our family members.

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:36.100
In all honesty, I wanted to
film this video yesterday,

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:39.190
but I was working a 12 hour
hospital shift seeing patients.

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:40.140
What did I learn?

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:41.940
There's truly a scarcity of supplies.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:44.990
N95 masks, which are
the properly fit masks

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:47.040
that we as health
professionals should be wearing

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:48.570
to decrease viral spread.

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:50.960
The surgical masks,
those inexpensive masks

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:52.080
you see on social media.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:53.580
We need our patients to wear those

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:54.840
so they don't get us sick.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:58.320
And finally, and the most
importantly, testing kits.

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:00.480
We need more testing kits.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:03.260
We need to be able to
identify who has COVID-19

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:05.420
and who has another virus
that's less important

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:06.630
in this given time.

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:09.750
Without testing kits, we can't
properly quarantine people,

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:11.710
and we're obviously quarantining people

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:14.790
that do not have COVID-19
and that's truly a problem.

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:17.930
So I call on the White House
Coronavirus Task Force,

00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:19.770
get us the equipment we
need on the front lines

00:04:19.770 --> 00:04:20.910
as health professionals

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:22.700
because the last thing we want to happen

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:26.000
is to have more doctors,
nurses, CMAs, PAs,

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:27.840
all of us on the front lines to get sick

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:30.410
and then not have anybody to
take care of our patients.

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:32.120
Let's go ahead and jump into the subject

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:34.840
that I'm most passionate
about, misinformation.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:38.710
- People die from the flu
and this is very unusual.

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:40.080
And it is a little bit different,

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:41.640
but in some ways it's easier

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.500
and in some ways it's
a little bit tougher.

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:46.370
- There are some similarities
between the flu and COVID-19

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:48.630
but there are very serious differences.

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:50.490
Similarities, they're both viruses,

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:52.220
they both spread through
respiratory droplets,

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:53.580
the symptoms are similar.

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:55.570
However the severity is quite different,

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:57.270
the lethality is quite different.

00:04:57.270 --> 00:05:00.410
And most importantly,
we do not have a vaccine

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:03.820
and we don't have an anti-viral
medication, FDA approved,

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:05.180
to treat COVID-19.

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:06.380
What does all that mean?

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:08.350
It means the lethality
rate is gonna be higher.

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:09.760
More people are gonna lose their lives

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:11.720
because of COVID-19 than the flu.

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:13.070
More people are gonna get infected

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:14.550
with COVID-19 than the flu

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:15.840
because it's more infectious.

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:18.090
Early research suggests
this virus can spread

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:21.500
two to three times faster
than the influenza virus.

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:24.450
This is why it's become a
pandemic in a matter of months.

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:26.700
There is a chain letter going around

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:29.850
titled "Information on Coronavirus".

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:31.750
I can't believe I'm even
saying the term chain letter,

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:34.020
but it is going around
via email and Twitter,

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:36.290
I saw even Brother Nature retweeted it

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:39.270
and it has like 114,000 retweets on it.

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:42.890
It has quote unquote Stanford
notes on Coronavirus.

00:05:42.890 --> 00:05:44.700
Stanford came out and
did a public message,

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:46.400
said they have nothing to do with this.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:49.400
Because this misinformation
is spreading like wildfire.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:50.990
Some of the things written in here.

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:54.190
Drinking warm water is
effective for all viruses.

00:05:54.190 --> 00:05:57.720
If you have a runny nose and
sputum, you have a common cold.

00:05:57.720 --> 00:06:00.120
It talks about a 10 second breathing test

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:02.290
that if you're able to hold
your breath for 10 seconds

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:04.940
you don't have the
novel coronavirus, what?

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:06.570
None of this is medically accurate

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:07.880
and this goes to show

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:10.480
that just because a celebrity
gets a lot of retweets

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:11.970
or likes on a given post,

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:14.190
it does not mean it's
accurate information.

00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:18.410
Trust the CDC, WHO, or trust
the health professionals

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:20.570
that are actually dealing
with this crisis head on.

00:06:20.570 --> 00:06:22.860
Let's talk about two
pieces of misinformation

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:24.640
that I think even some medical experts

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:26.520
have gotten themselves confused over.

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:28.960
One is about using certain supplements

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:31.430
to help prevent or treat
the novel coronavirus,

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:33.140
zinc being a primary example.

00:06:33.140 --> 00:06:34.930
Yes, there was a study that showed

00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:37.300
zinc interrupts replication of this virus,

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:38.133
which is a good thing.

00:06:38.133 --> 00:06:40.540
However, very important, if
you actually read the study,

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:44.800
it shows that the zinc needed
to be inside your actual cells

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:46.970
not just in your bloodstream
or in your stomach,

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:48.100
in the cells.

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:51.260
The way that the research
got the zinc into the cells,

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:53.080
was through a zinc ionophore.

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:54.770
It's basically like a little tunnel

00:06:54.770 --> 00:06:56.700
that allowed the zinc to enter the cell

00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:59.540
then it interfered with the
viral replication, good stuff.

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:01.760
However, taking a zinc lozenge

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:05.440
does not create a zinc
gateway, a zinc ionophore,

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:06.990
to enter into our cells.

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:09.030
So no, taking zinc by mouth

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:11.560
does not disrupt the viral replication.

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:14.730
This is why we need to be very
careful when we read research

00:07:14.730 --> 00:07:17.260
to actually read it, not
just skim over the abstract.

00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:19.620
Next, let's move on to
surface contamination.

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:23.250
How long does the novel
coronavirus live on surfaces?

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:24.540
There's been some really good research

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:25.650
coming out in this area,

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:27.320
and the range that we're seeing

00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:31.570
is from hours to a day or
two, sometimes three days

00:07:31.570 --> 00:07:34.580
if we see perfect temperature, humidity,

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:36.120
and surface conditions.

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:39.810
This virus does live longer
on plastic and steel surfaces,

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:41.260
meaning non-porous ones.

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:43.280
So you want to be sure to be wiping down

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:47.100
commonly used surfaces, like
keyboards, like faucets.

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:48.690
That's obviously very important,

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:50.500
but the doctors that are
going out there and saying

00:07:50.500 --> 00:07:52.450
that it lasts one to two weeks.

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:55.900
Practically speaking, especially
outdoors, that's not true.

00:07:55.900 --> 00:07:57.043
And in the one study that came out

00:07:57.043 --> 00:07:59.110
talking about this 9 day period,

00:07:59.110 --> 00:08:01.790
it was for a very specific
sub-strain of this virus,

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:04.110
it does not apply to
the majority of cases.

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:05.600
Also I'm gonna reiterate,

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:08.670
the primary driver of
how this virus spreads

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:10.630
is through respiratory droplets.

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:12.620
Meaning that you inhale them,

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:15.350
you touch your mouth, eyes, or nose.

00:08:15.350 --> 00:08:18.740
So surface contamination is
a possible way to spread it,

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:21.380
but the main one is those
aerosolized particles.

00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:22.820
It doesn't mean it's airborne,

00:08:22.820 --> 00:08:24.580
because it's not technically airborne,

00:08:24.580 --> 00:08:26.140
it's aerosolized particles

00:08:26.140 --> 00:08:28.410
that are temporarily hanging in the air.

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:29.780
That's what I call germ hang time.

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:31.190
That's why in the winter time,

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:32.820
there's a higher chance you get sick,

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:34.160
'cause the air is drier,

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:36.500
more germs hanging in the air
for a longer period of time,

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:37.500
easier to get sick.

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:39.570
The longest that we've
seen them hanging around,

00:08:39.570 --> 00:08:41.730
three hours for this novel coronavirus.

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:44.380
So it is possible to walk into a room

00:08:44.380 --> 00:08:46.210
that's empty where
someone's sneezed before

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:48.460
and inhale some of these
respiratory droplets,

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:50.340
but outdoors that's not something

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:51.360
you should be concerned about.

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:53.230
Because the sun, with its UV rays,

00:08:53.230 --> 00:08:54.940
is our most powerful disinfectant.

00:08:54.940 --> 00:08:57.730
Let's move on and talk about
a common conspiracy question

00:08:57.730 --> 00:08:58.730
that I've been getting asked.

00:08:58.730 --> 00:09:01.480
Did this virus come out of a lab in China?

00:09:01.480 --> 00:09:03.280
If conspiracy theorists believe

00:09:03.280 --> 00:09:05.050
that this is a bio terrorism weapon,

00:09:05.050 --> 00:09:06.000
it's a really bad one.

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:07.530
'Cause it's crushed the Chinese economy

00:09:07.530 --> 00:09:09.650
as well as the international economy.

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:11.770
It has a very low lethality rate

00:09:11.770 --> 00:09:13.400
for something that's
considered to be deadly.

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:15.940
If it escaped out of a lab in China,

00:09:15.940 --> 00:09:18.290
which we have no evidence for that.

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:20.900
It does not change anything
that we have to do now

00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:21.850
to protect ourselves.

00:09:21.850 --> 00:09:23.260
You wanna talk about after the fact,

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:25.470
once we're investigating this virus, cool.

00:09:25.470 --> 00:09:27.940
But right now, we need
to take actionable steps

00:09:27.940 --> 00:09:29.630
to stay alert not anxious,

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:32.580
be educated, and protect
ourselves and our family members.

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:34.420
Let's move on to potential treatments

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:36.720
because that's what I'm
most optimistic about.

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:39.740
There are well over 300 clinical
trials ongoing right now.

00:09:39.740 --> 00:09:41.760
And that's a good and bad thing.

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:43.570
Bad because there's some medications

00:09:43.570 --> 00:09:45.260
that shouldn't be tested, are.

00:09:45.260 --> 00:09:47.160
And it's taking away from the patient pool

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:48.700
that can be enrolled in these studies.

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:50.800
Good because we're getting
a lot of different options

00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:51.870
tested all at once.

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:53.470
Leading the way, Remdesivir.

00:09:53.470 --> 00:09:55.100
It's an anti-viral medication

00:09:55.100 --> 00:09:57.350
that was primarily used to treat Ebola.

00:09:57.350 --> 00:09:58.183
The way that it works

00:09:58.183 --> 00:10:00.700
is interrupts the viruses
replication cycle.

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:02.570
Let's think back, how does a virus work?

00:10:02.570 --> 00:10:03.860
It infects your cell,

00:10:03.860 --> 00:10:07.140
then it hijacks the cells
own inside machinery

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:08.340
and replicates itself.

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:09.810
We wanna stop that process

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:11.290
to prevent the virus from spreading.

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:13.230
Hopefully Remdesivir does that.

00:10:13.230 --> 00:10:15.500
Other medications that
we have being tested,

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:17.550
HIV medications like Kaletra,

